        "answer": "Creates movement/reset/measurement helpers; defaults start/end delay2500ms, auto speed0.4, stick speed0.7, auto on/stick off. Resets accumulators now, wraps setText to recalculate, then schedules a zero-delay setup callback. That callback measures/resets and creates one100ms update timer if absent. Tick handles stick priority, start delay, auto motion, clamping, end delay and reset, then invokes movement helper (reversed-language coordinates preserved). Speeds divide by timeElapsed as written; no zero-time guard, subscription unregister or close wrapper is added.",
